# Live API Safety Rule

The global rule `~/.cursor/rules/no-live-api-without-consent.mdc` is authoritative and always applies in this project.

Project-specific examples include:

- Anthropic Claude calls from the LLM assessment pipeline.
- Connector calls to EFEHR, EGDI, Overpass, Corine, NOAA, ERA5, WDPA, and similar services.
- Any batch enrichment command that reaches third-party APIs.

Dry runs and local-only database or file inspection remain allowed without additional consent.
